1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,140
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,221
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,760
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:09,937
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,460
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,957
We'll get past every
wall that's in our wake!

7
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:15,697
Go without hesitation!

8
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,860
Hands up!

9
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

10
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,197
To get to the answers we're looking for.

11
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:34,897
We came to this new world
believing that surely someday.

12
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:37,957
We just might find the way.

13
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

14
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,377
Our bonds won't waver.

15
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

16
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,920
Let's head on towards.

17
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,717
A bright new future.

18
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

19
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,557
Sing about what you are dreaming.

20
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,197
Always stand up.

21
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:02,417
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

22
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

23
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

24
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,420
Let's head on never stopping.

25
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:11,377
Only look up.

26
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,397
Keep your head up. Way up high.

27
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:15,077
Always step up.

28
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,977
If waves erupt up to the sky.

29
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:19,397
Never give up. Our wishes.

30
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,757
They will come together.

31
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:21,977
And lead us on.

32
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:23,180
For the future.

33
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:26,217
We drift on.

34
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:27,837
Riding the waves.

35
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,457
Towards another shore.

36
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:30,717
Day by day.

37
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,317
There are many meetings.

38
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,517
Many goodbyes.

39
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:37,860
Underneath the flag. We fly.

40
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:42,457
I'll remember.

41
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:45,877
The pain within, I'll keep
it in my heart forever.

42
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:49,837
And never take it lightly,
but I won't surrender.

43
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom, I will keep in mind.

44
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,597
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

45
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

46
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,497
Sing about what you are dreaming.

47
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:03,357
Always stand up, raise up
the flag that you believe in.

48
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:07,237
Gotta keep up, we'll get past
everyone that's in our way.

49
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,820
Let's head on, never stop it.

50
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:14,337
Only look up, keep your
head up way up high.

51
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:17,937
Always step up, if waves are
rough, jump through the sky.

52
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:21,677
Never give up, our wishes
they will come together.

53
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,140
And lead us on for the future.

54
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:26,140
Hands up.

55
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,200
Listen up, you pirate scum!

56
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:37,177
The tanker is your territory
and you better stay on it!

57
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:40,077
This line here is the division
between good and evil.

58
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,866
So don't you even dare
think of crossing over.

59
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:45,333
Them's the rules to live by, Straw Hats.

60
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:51,857
Where the hell did you get an
idea to waste your time with this?

61
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:52,770
Huh?

62
00:02:52,853 --> 00:02:56,337
The only thing I told you to do was
not fraternize with the pirates.

63
00:02:56,420 --> 00:02:58,337
And there's no better way to enforce that.

64
00:02:58,420 --> 00:02:59,597
Men will respect the line.

65
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:02,737
We done determined that the line
don't applicate to the medics, though.

66
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:05,137
I got into contact with the G5 base.

67
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:08,680
We're gonna wait right here
for them to pick us up. Sir!

68
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:11,380
What? That's nuts!

69
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:13,617
Don't turn yourself in, Brownbeard!

70
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:16,737
Seems like a waste since you
and my crew are friends now.

71
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:17,650
Ha-ha-ha!

72
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:22,377
Turns out Caesar was exposing his men to
small amounts of poison this whole time.

73
00:03:22,460 --> 00:03:25,897
But they said the government will
treat us if we hand ourselves over.

74
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:27,140
Okay, fair enough.

75
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,145
Hey, what the hell, Straw Hat?

76
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:32,162
I just told you not to
step across the damn line!

77
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:33,837
Clean out your filthy ears!

78
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:35,040
Why should I care?

79
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:37,220
That's your stupid rule, not mine.

80
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:43,200
Anyway, I figure I would rather rot in
prison than die of Caesar's guinea pig.

81
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:50,017
But, kid, I can't tell you how good
it felt to watch you clock Caesar.

82
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,260
Thank you, Luffy.

83
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:53,640
One, two, three!

84
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:57,480
Come on, go with all your might!

85
00:03:57,780 --> 00:04:01,057
I really wish somebody told me we
were going to be using this tanker.

86
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:02,797
I knew we were going to have to fix it.

87
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:06,115
Well, I would have found
another place to brawl it out.

88
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,350
Huh?

89
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,897
What's with the screaming?

90
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:16,098
Chop, are you okay?

91
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:18,340
Help me! Huh?

92
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,880
You've got to stop him, hurry!

93
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:22,450
So, what?

94
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,020
He's committing murder!

95
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:28,450
What?

96
00:04:28,533 --> 00:04:29,378
Who's the murderer?

97
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,799
Who the heck are you talking about?

98
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:34,880
Law is killing them!

99
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:36,040
Really, Traffy?

100
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:39,804
And why is Brooke freaking out?

101
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:42,220
I also committed a murder.

102
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:45,600
I mean, Keenumon was already dead, but...

103
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:48,360
I shattered his body!

104
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,017
He's dead and you shattered him?

105
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:54,297
You killed him again?

106
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:55,797
I don't want you to fix him.

107
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:56,877
What do you mean, fix him?

108
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:58,857
He was already dead before you broke him.

109
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:00,457
What if we glue him back together?

110
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:03,069
How are you two not
getting that he's dead?

111
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,380
You're supposed to be dead!

112
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:11,840
Why are you attacking him, Sanji?

113
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:13,022
Why wouldn't I?

114
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:16,077
We were just discussing how
he's dead, and now he's not.

115
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:18,497
You should be happy about
it, not kicking him.

116
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:20,800
It was a reflex. Jeez, sorry.

117
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,437
Well, it is a surprise.

118
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:23,837
Are you guys seeing this?

119
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:26,979
The guy who they thought
was killed is really alive?

120
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:30,560
Oh, I'm so utterly relieved, Kin'emon.

121
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:33,360
I thought you were gone for good. Father!

122
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:38,390
Momonosuke!

123
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,270
Father!

124
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,130
Momonosuke!

125
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:50,340
I feared that I would never see you again.

126
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,440
And I thought you were dead.

127
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,350
Huh?

128
00:05:55,433 --> 00:05:56,420
That kid's Momo?

129
00:05:57,340 --> 00:06:00,399
Oh yeah, he said something
about being a human once.

130
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:02,870
Huh?

131
00:06:02,953 --> 00:06:05,115
He is not normally this naked, though.

132
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,400
And poof!

133
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:17,380
This kimono suits you quite splendidly.

134
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:19,760
Just like a true son of Wado.

135
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,220
Tell me, father.

136
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,157
How did you know that I...

137
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,220
was...

138
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,350
Momonosuke!

139
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,000
Get out here now!

140
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:33,740
You sicko!

141
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:36,197
How could you do that to those poor kids?

142
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:39,456
I saw what you were doing
and you are gonna regret it!

143
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:43,385
There's a reason I told
you not to look inside.

144
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:45,853
I had a feeling you wouldn't understand.

145
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:47,760
Why I would slice them up.

146
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:49,137
Oh, there's drugs.

147
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:53,044
This was the fastest way to get
that poison out of their systems.

148
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:56,440
Look, the raccoon's here! Hey, Mr.

149
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:58,758
Raccoon Wait, you guys are all okay?

150
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:03,237
The guy with the big puffy
hat just came to see us.

151
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,377
He cut the bad drugs out of our bodies.

152
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:06,537
It was crazy.

153
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:11,177
I was real scared at first,
but I feel awesome now.

154
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:13,937
He chopped us up into little
pieces and it was real funny.

155
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:15,320
I'm hungry now.

156
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:17,297
He was helping them.

157
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:20,777
I'm kind of worried, though,
because Mocha still hasn't woken up.

158
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:24,036
She was fighting to try to
save all of us, wasn't she?

159
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,877
The master was always so nice.

160
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:28,097
I had no idea he was such a bad guy.

161
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:32,677
My memory's fuzzy, but I remember when
Mocha coughed her blood and passed out.

162
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:33,590
Hey, Mr.

163
00:07:33,673 --> 00:07:35,361
Raccoon, I'm actually a reindeer.

164
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,300
Mocha, she'll be okay, right?

165
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,325
Can she still go home with us?

166
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,720
Please say yes.

167
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:41,879
Of course she can.

168
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:43,140
You're safe now.

169
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:45,086
The nightmare's finally over.

170
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:48,277
Where's the lady with the orange hair?

171
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:51,057
Yeah, she promised that she was
going to help us all get home.

172
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:54,957
And after everything she's done for
us, we wanted to tell her thanks.

173
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:55,870
Hey, kids?

174
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,673
Let's get you all home.

175
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:02,837
The Navy's going to take you back
to your parents, safe and sound.

176
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:05,155
But we don't want to go with the Navy!

177
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:07,160
What about the robot?

178
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:08,720
And the stretchy guy?

179
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,704
Or the guy with weird eyebrows?

180
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,320
Mmm, smells good. What?

181
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:15,577
I wonder what Sanji's cooking up for us.

182
00:08:15,660 --> 00:08:16,490
I'm starving.

183
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:18,180
There we go.

184
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:19,857
That's looking pretty straight to me.

185
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:23,720
Just needs a super quick fix
and it'll be good to go. Nami?

186
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:30,040
Did you manage to sort out
a deal with the Marines?

187
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:32,030
Yep.

188
00:08:32,113 --> 00:08:34,177
I'm going to leave the
children in their hands.

189
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:36,477
I talked to Big Game about saving them,

190
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:41,337
but I kind of doubt their parents would
be too keen on pirates bringing them home.

191
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,637
Yeah, you got a point.

192
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:46,537
I think we've dealt with enough wrongful
accusations of kidnapping in our lives.

193
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:49,717
Might as well just let the
good guys take all the credit.

194
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:50,760
Like always.

195
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:52,170
Besides.

196
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,694
I have a bad history with most Marines,

197
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:58,217
but if they're women,
it's a different story.

198
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:00,000
Yeah? Why's that?

199
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:03,800
Well, they make me feel safe

200
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:07,560
Oh yeah, your mom was in the Navy, right?

201
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:09,427
Don't know how I forgot that

202
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:11,737
She was, but that's beside the point.

203
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:14,644
You can always count on
a strong female soldier.

204
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,280
Ain't that the truth.

205
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,340
It sounds gross when you say it.

206
00:09:20,880 --> 00:09:22,300
I was just agreeing.

207
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,100
New Kama Kimpo technique.

208
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,800
99 fundamental recipes.

209
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:32,574
A cold, exhausted body needs a healthy
heaping helping of fat and warmth.

210
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:36,480
So I made hormone soup du
Giri with sea pig pork.

211
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:41,749
I know you've been running on
an empty stomach for days now.

212
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:44,992
So start with the soup and eat it slowly.

213
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,600
I want it now!

214
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:55,160
I bet you're starving, aren't you?

215
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:58,400
You're so lucky, Sanji's the best cook.

216
00:10:01,220 --> 00:10:02,680
I do not want this!

217
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,897
You cannot force me to
eat your strange food!

218
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:06,760
Hold it right there, punk.

219
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,877
The hell are you doing with that bowl?

220
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,377
I don't care if you're a kid.

221
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:12,077
Anyone wastes food around me?

222
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:13,572
Well, then I waste them.

223
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:16,340
I gladly accept your fee. What?

224
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:22,620
Uh, hey. Delicious! What is this?

225
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:24,153
My streak is returning.

226
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:28,651
These delicacies you've prepared
are shockingly delectable.

227
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:30,200
My father!

228
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,860
Their food is fine to eat, son.

229
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:34,554
Accept their kindness.

230
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:36,617
My life was saved on this island,

231
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:40,157
and they were the ones who saved it—it was

232
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,977
a gift to have met such
trustworthy people!

233
00:10:42,060 --> 00:10:46,477
All this time, you haven't had
a single bite to eat, have you?

234
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:48,437
Such a strong boy!

235
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:50,957
It must have been awful!

236
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:55,877
You have nothing to worry about anymore.

237
00:10:55,960 --> 00:11:02,077
We must have faith that everyone
else is alive and well now.

238
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:05,457
Let us choose to live!

239
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:06,857
You hear me, momonosuke!

240
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:07,770
It's

241
00:11:22,020 --> 00:11:22,857
that good!

242
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:25,237
It's tasty enough to cry! Moron!

243
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:27,397
They've clearly gone through some crap!

244
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:30,157
What the hell happened
to those two? Hello!

245
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:36,537
What happened to your sacred

246
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:38,377
boundary between good and evil?

247
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:39,290
You jerks!

248
00:11:39,373 --> 00:11:40,717
We're calling for a ceasefire!

249
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:45,297
Well, if that's the case—that's
the booth from the tanker!

250
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:46,477
We're on it!

251
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:49,897
We need to talk, Straw Hat!

252
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:52,297
There's no time to stick around and eat!

253
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:54,337
They're gonna be right on our tail!

254
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,297
We've got to.

255
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:56,380
got to leave now.

256
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:57,360
That bat huh?

257
00:11:57,860 --> 00:11:59,697
Tell your crew we've got a ship out.

258
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:00,721
Alright I'll let

259
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:10,650
him know.

260
00:12:10,733 --> 00:12:11,563
Listen up guys.

261
00:12:11,646 --> 00:12:12,837
See you again and get down.

262
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:13,750
Cheers.

263
00:12:13,833 --> 00:12:14,663
Is something wrong?

264
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:19,937
But father the true warriors shouldn't
allow themselves to weep in front of others.

265
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:21,020
